The CUnit test suite hardcodes a macOS-specific absolute path to prelude.lisp,
so the tests only run on the original developer's machine. They must be as
portable as bocl itself: build and run on every POSIX system without editing.

STATUS: open.  Found 2026-06-28 while validating the DRIBBLE work in a Linux
container: 31 of the CUnit tests could not run because their suite-setup loads
the prelude from a path that does not exist off the author's Mac.

== Symptom ==
Every prelude-dependent test does, in its TEST_SUITE_SETUP:

    bocl_load_cstring("/Users/pjb/src/public/bocl/bootstrap/prelude.lisp");

On any machine where that absolute path does not exist the prelude fails to
load, so the whole suite errors out (undefined functions etc.).  Affected
files (31): test_clos, test_control, test_destructuring, test_format,
test_list_utils, test_loop, test_misc, test_numeric_extras, test_restarts,
test_seq_lib, test_setf, test_strings, test_structures, and
test_slice15..18,20..33.

== Cause ==
The prelude path is a literal string baked into each test's source, pointing at
the author's home directory layout.  Nothing derives it from the build tree, an
environment variable, or a compile-time setting.

== Non-issues (do NOT "fix") ==
  - The "/usr/local/..." strings in test_slice17 and test_slice32 are pathname
    *parsing* test data (string literals fed to PATHNAME-NAME, MERGE-PATHNAMES,
    logical-pathname translations).  They never touch the filesystem and are
    portable as-is.
  - The Makefile's -I/opt/local (macOS/MacPorts) and -I/usr/local (FreeBSD
    ports) CUnit search paths are already guarded by $(UNAME) conditionals;
    that is the correct, portable way to locate a platform's CUnit.

== Policy ==
Tests must not hardcode anything that breaks on a different system: no absolute
home paths, no OS-specific assumptions outside properly-guarded Makefile
conditionals.  Prefer (in order): an environment-variable override, a
compile-time path derived from the build tree, then a sensible relative
fallback.

== Fix sketch ==
  - Add a shared helper bocl_test_load_prelude() in tests/simple_test.c
    (already linked into every test) that locates prelude.lisp by trying, in
    order: getenv("BOCL_PRELUDE"); a compile-time BOCL_TEST_PRELUDE_PATH define; the
    relative paths "../bootstrap/prelude.lisp" and "bootstrap/prelude.lisp";
    using access(R_OK) to pick the first that exists, and erroring clearly if
    none do.
  - Have tests/Makefile pass the build-tree path:
        CFLAGS += -DBOCL_TEST_PRELUDE_PATH='"$(abspath ../bootstrap/prelude.lisp)"'
  - Replace all 31 hardcoded bocl_load_cstring("/Users/pjb/.../prelude.lisp")
    calls with bocl_test_load_prelude().

== Acceptance ==
  - A fresh checkout builds and runs `make -C tests test` on Linux/*BSD/macOS
    with no source edits and no machine-specific path.
  - BOCL_PRELUDE=/path/to/prelude.lisp overrides the location at run time.

== DONE (2026-06-28, v1.4.7) ==
Implemented exactly as in the fix sketch:
  - tests/simple_test.c: new bocl_test_load_prelude() — tries $BOCL_PRELUDE,
    then compile-time BOCL_TEST_PRELUDE_PATH, then "../bootstrap/prelude.lisp"
    and "bootstrap/prelude.lisp"; picks the first readable via access(R_OK);
    exits EX_NOINPUT with a clear message if none found.  It calls
    bocl_load_prelude() (NOT bocl_load_cstring): binds *PACKAGE* to COMMON-LISP
    and loads cl-exports.lisp first, so the reader's bare symbols match eval.c's
    S(DEFMACRO)/S(...) caches.  (The 31 tests had used the raw loader, so they
    were doubly broken: wrong path AND wrong loader.)
  - tests/simple_test.h: declaration + doc.
  - tests/Makefile: CFLAGS += -DBOCL_TEST_PRELUDE_PATH='"$(abspath
    ../bootstrap/prelude.lisp)"' (distinct from the install-path macro
    BOCL_PRELUDE_PATH in sources/common.mk — do not confuse them).
  - Replaced all 31 hardcoded bocl_load_cstring("/Users/pjb/.../prelude.lisp")
    with bocl_test_load_prelude().

Validated on Linux (this container has libcunit): clean compile (no warnings);
prelude now loads; ~12 suites produce real CUnit summaries where before none of
the 31 could even load (5 pass clean: test_destructuring, test_loop,
test_numeric_extras, test_structures, test_slice23).  Confirmed cwd-independent
(ran from /tmp — compile-time abspath resolved it) and $BOCL_PRELUDE override
honoured.

Residual per-suite failures (ABORTs, behavioural mismatches) are NOT portability
issues — they are identical on every platform and are tracked separately in
stale-test-suite-failures.issue.
